course: dictionary
lesson: 6077
title: Messenger: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A messenger is a person who carries a message, letter or parcel from one person or place to another. Long ago, this was often the only way news could travel. «Before telephones, messages went by letter, by messenger, or by telegraph.»
explain: The same word can mean different things, so look at the words around it. «Don't shoot the messenger» is a saying about a person who brings bad news, and it means do not blame that person. Context tells you which meaning to use.
explain: In science, a messenger can be something you cannot see. «The aches all over in flu come mostly from the immune system's chemical messengers.» Here a messenger is a substance in the body that carries signals. Does the first meaning, a person with a parcel, fit this sentence? No, so the science meaning is the right one.
explain: Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If it does not, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: A messenger carries a message, letter or parcel from one person or place to another.
fact: «Messenger» can also mean an app or service for sending text messages.
fact: In science, a messenger is a substance in the body that carries signals, such as a hormone.
fact: «The Romans built about 80,000 kilometres of straight, paved roads so armies and messengers could move fast.»
fact: Before telephones, messages went by letter, by messenger, or by telegraph, which sent coded clicks along wires.
exercise: «The Romans built roads so armies and messengers could move fast.» Who are the messengers in this sentence? | Bags for carrying school books | Roads with stones on them | Horses that pull carts | *People who carry messages from place to place
exercise: Ravi sends a text on Messenger. What does Messenger mean here? | *An app for sending text messages | A large bag for shopping | A person who carries letters | A substance in the body
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you how fast the Romans wanted messengers to move. | paved | roads | straight | *fast
test: «Don't shoot the messenger» is a saying. What does it mean? | Send your letters by post only | Always run very fast | *Do not blame the person who brings bad news | Do not hurt any animals
test: «Prophets were messengers who spoke God's word: they warned kings and people about injustice.» What kind of messengers were prophets? | *People who carried God's words to kings and people |
